 58824, a gap of at least 601 units, exceeding the 600-unit relay limit; the alternative in-edge 1514->1517 has no event anywhere near that time. Thus the terminal segment of any candidate path is already broken, and the upstream hops from 695 are tens of thousands of units too early. Large overall volume and hub popularity (steps 01, 05, 08) explain the static reachability but not a temporal cascade."}, "raw_final_response": "**Conclusion: no time-respecting cascade exists.**\n\nKey reasoning chain:\n- 695 has a single outgoing edge in the window: 695\u21921468 (step_03), occurring in [31225, 34424] (step_14/20/24 bisection).\n- 1495 has a single incoming edge: 1517\u21921495 (step_04), occurring in [60025, 61624] (steps 19, 21, 25, 26) \u2014 roughly 27,000 time units after 695's only broadcast.\n- The only way in to 1517 near that time is 1474\u21921517, in [59425, 61624] (step_27, step_31); 1514\u21921517 has no event in that neighbourhood (step_28).\n- 1474's sole in-neighbour is 1134 (step_09), and 1134\u21921474 occurs at or before 58824 (steps 29, 32), i.e. at least 601 units before the earliest possible 1474\u21921517 event \u2014 the 600-unit relay constraint is violated, so the final approach path is broken regardless of upstream activity.\n- Upstream (695\u21921468\u2192274\u21921134, steps 22, 23, 30) is orderable only across tens of thousands of units, far beyond the 600-unit latency limit.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"t_636b848d\",\n  \"decision\": \"absent\",\n  \"mechanism\": \"cascade\",\n  \"entities\": [695, 1495, 1468, 274, 1134, 1474, 1517],\n  \"window\": [28025, 66424],\n  \"confidence\": 0.79,\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_03\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_04\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_14\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_20\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_24\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_19\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_25\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_26\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_07\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_27\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_31\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_28\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_09\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_29\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_32\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_22\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_23\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_30\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_01\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_05\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_08\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"}\n  ],\n  \"narrative\": \"Static connectivity between 695 and 1495 exists (both sit in a large 2-3 hop component through hubs 1468/274/800), but the timing does not support influence transfer. 695 emits only one event (695->1468) around t\u224831k-34k, while the unique event that reaches 1495 (1517->1495) happens around t\u224860k-61.6k. The only feasible predecessor of that event, 1474->1517 (>=59425), is itself preceded by 1134->1474 no later than 58824, a gap of at least 601 units, exceeding the 600-unit relay limit; the alternative in-edge 1514->1517 has no event anywhere near that time. Thus the terminal segment of any candidate path is already broken, and the upstream hops from 695 are tens of thousands of units too early. Large overall volume and hub popularity (steps 01, 05, 08) explain the static reachability but not a temporal cascade.\"\n}\n```", "total_input_tokens": 110641, "total_output_tokens": 10605, "total_tokens": 121246, "total_latency_ms": 157251, "llm_calls": 13, "schema_repairs": 0, "status": "succes